{
  "name": "Chart end markers",
  "description": "Each highlighted end of a chart draws its own marker. The first three layers store only the shared `marker`, so each end is derived from it: none draws nothing at either end, dot draws a dot at both, pointer draws a triangle over the highest and a dot over the lowest. The fourth layer is the pair the shared setting cannot say, the highest painted red with no marker and the lowest bright green with a dot, so it writes `marker` as dot and both per-end keys. The fifth draws a triangle at both ends. The last two store a marker for an end their highlight does not cover, and it resolves to none: highlight Highest ignores a stored lowest triangle, and highlight Lowest ignores the triangle the pointer implies for the highest. All seven read 3, 9, 1, 5, so the highest is reading 1 and the lowest is reading 2.",
